{
  "root_cause": "The fieldset disables its child controls, but the focus‑trap’s tabble detection only checks the element’s own disabled property. Consequently the disabled speed select is mistakenly treated as the first tabbable node; attempting to focus it fails, leaving focus on the trigger button.",
  "repair_strategy": "Move the disabled attribute from the fieldset to the speed select element so the select is correctly reported as disabled and skipped by the focus trap, allowing focus to land on the street input.",
  "expected_accessibility_effect": "Keyboard users opening the dialog will now receive focus on the first usable field (the street input) as required.",
  "functional_risks": [
    "The speed select remains disabled until an address is saved, preserving the intended UI; no functional change besides correct focus order."
  ],
  "verification_requirements": [
    "After opening the dialog with Enter, focus must be on #street.",
    "Typing an address and pressing Save updates the status to 'Delivering to <address>'.",
    "Escape closes the dialog and returns focus to the #open button."
  ]
}
